{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba window_test.py'","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The whole-window measurement of the linking version (poc-v119) against old-2 (poc-v118, 2026-07-01..09-20), D699.\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 window_test.py neither <scratch>      # $0: poc-v119 over the whole window, every link question answered \"neither\", every\n     4\t                                                #     other request from a copy of old-2's archive; the result must equal old-2\n     5\t  python3 window_test.py census-dry <scratch>   # $0: the census pass with every eligible pair answered \"reads\"; must stay old-2\n     6\t  python3 window_test.py census <scratch> <draw> <ledger>   # paid (Jev only, ceiling $0.10): the same pass with each link job sent\n     7\t                                                #     to Jev and no link written, so the replay stays old-2; one draw of the link decisions\n     8\t\n     9\tThe `neither` pass proves that poc-v119 without links is old-2 over all 1,884 articles (DESIGN.md table 3, first row, extended from the\n    10\tJuly prefix to the whole window), and lists every link question the version would ask: each opening of a number question with the\n    11\tnumber questions it was shown, the pairs eligible under D695, and the pairs not eligible with their reason.\n    12\t\"\"\"\n    13\timport json\n    14\timport shutil\n    15\timport sqlite3\n    16\timport sys\n    17\timport time\n    18\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    19\t\n    20\tREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n    21\tJULY = REPO / 'docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design'\n    22\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    23\tsys.path.insert(0, str(JULY))\n    24\tfrom hivemind import config, model, replay, universe       # noqa: E402\n    25\timport july_test                                            # noqa: E402\n    26\timport rebuild_control                                      # noqa: E402\n    27\t\n    28\tOLD2 = july_test.OLD2\n    29\tITEMS = july_test.ITEMS\n    30\tV119 = july_test.V119\n    31\tUNIVERSE = july_test.UNIVERSE\n    32\tWINDOW = ('2026-07-01', '2026-09-20')\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef refused_rows():\n    36\t    \"\"\"old-2's answers its own run refused (the archive keeps them under the request's hash with a ':refused:' suffix, so no later\n    37\t    identical request is answered with them): {request hash: stored provider response}. A replay must meet each refusal again to\n    38\t    reach the stored retry.\"\"\"\n    39\t    stored = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    40\t    return {sha.split(':refused:')[0]: json.loads(response) for sha, response in\n    41\t            stored.execute(\"select request_sha256, response_json from model_calls where request_sha256 like '%:refused:%' order by call_id\")}\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\tdef replay_window(folder, link_answer):\n    45\t    \"\"\"poc-v119 from an empty ledger over the whole window: link questions go to `link_answer`; every other request must be answered\n    46\t    from the copy of old-2's archive (an answer old-2's own run refused is given back once, so the check refuses it again); anything\n    47\t    else stops the pass. Returns the census: equality with old-2, every link job, every opening with its pairs.\"\"\"\n    48\t    if folder.exists():\n    49\t        raise SystemExit(f'{folder} exists: a pass starts from an empty folder')\n    50\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True)\n    51\t    shutil.copyfile(OLD2 / 'archive.sqlite', folder / 'archive.sqlite')\n    52\t    asked, refused_again = [], []\n    53\t    stored_refusals = refused_rows()\n    54\t\n    55\t    def transport(*args):\n    56\t        if len(args) == 1 and july_test.is_link_request(args[0]):\n    57\t            asked.append(sorted(args[0]['questions']))\n    58\t            return link_answer(args[0])\n    59\t        response = stored_refusals.pop(model.request_identity(args[-1])[1], None)\n    60\t        if response is not None:                   # old-2's own run refused this answer: give it back, so the check refuses it again\n    61\t            refused_again.append(model.request_identity(args[-1])[1][:12])\n    62\t            return response\n    63\t        (folder / 'missed-request.json').write_text(json.dumps(args[-1], ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\n    64\t        raise july_test.Stop('a request other than a link question missed the archive')\n    65\t    started = time.time()\n    66\t    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=str(ITEMS), views_path=str(folder / 'views.sqlite'), archive=model.Archive(str(folder / 'archive.sqlite')),\n    67\t                        cfg=config.load(str(V119)), universe=universe.load(str(UNIVERSE)), from_day=WINDOW[0], until_day=WINDOW[1],\n    68\t                        transport=transport, log=lambda *a: None, only_objects={'NVDA'})\n    69\t    print('totals:', totals, 'seconds:', round(time.time() - started))\n    70\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    71\t    last_seq = conn.execute('select max(seq) from days_completed').fetchone()[0]\n    72\t    stored_last = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True).execute('select max(seq) from days_completed').fetchone()[0]\n    73\t    print('last completed seq', last_seq, 'old-2', stored_last)\n    74\t    equal = last_seq == stored_last and rebuild_control.compare(folder / 'views.sqlite', last_seq)\n    75\t    openings = []\n    76\t    for attempt, seq, status, record_json in conn.execute('select attempt_id, seq, status, record_json from link_selections order by id'):\n    77\t        record = json.loads(record_json)\n    78\t        if status == 'proposed' and record.get('pairs'):\n    79\t            openings.append({'attempt': attempt, 'seq': seq, 'pairs': record['pairs'], 'calls': record.get('calls', []),\n    80\t                             'proposed': record.get('proposed', []), 'corrections': record.get('corrections', [])})\n    81\t    census = {'equal to old-2': equal, 'link jobs asked': len(asked), 'questions in them': sum(len(a) for a in asked),\n    82\t              \"old-2's refused answers met again\": refused_again, 'left unmet': sorted(sha[:12] for sha in stored_refusals),\n    83\t              'link rows written': conn.execute(\"select count(*) from dependencies where kind='reads'\").fetchone()[0],\n    84\t              'openings with a pair shown': openings}\n    85\t    (folder / 'census.json').write_text(json.dumps(census, indent=1))\n    86\t    print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in census.items() if k != 'openings with a pair shown'}, indent=1))\n    87\t    for opening in openings:\n    88\t        eligible = [p['thesis'] for p in opening['pairs'] if p.get('eligible')]\n    89\t        print(opening['seq'], 'eligible', eligible, 'not eligible', len(opening['pairs']) - len(eligible))\n    90\t    return census\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\tdef neither(scratch):\n    94\t    return replay_window(scratch / 'neither-v119', july_test.fake_jev(set()))['equal to old-2']\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\tCENSUS_CEILING = 0.10\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\tclass Everything:\n   101\t    def __contains__(self, item):\n   102\t        return True\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\tdef without_links(run):\n   106\t    \"\"\"Run `run()` with the writer handed no proposed link (the census's only change to the product path).\"\"\"\n   107\t    from hivemind.views import writing\n   108\t    original_write = writing.write\n   109\t\n   110\t    def write_without_links(*args, **keywords):\n   111\t        keywords['proposed_links'] = None\n   112\t        return original_write(*args, **keywords)\n   113\t    writing.write = write_without_links\n   114\t    try:\n   115\t        return run()\n   116\t    finally:\n   117\t        writing.write = original_write\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\tdef census_dry(scratch):\n   121\t    \"\"\"$0: the census pass with a fake Jev that answers every eligible pair \"the THESIS reads the CANDIDATE\", sign together (the\n   122\t    largest number of proposals); with the writer handed no link, the pass must still end equal to old-2 with no link row.\"\"\"\n   123\t    result = without_links(lambda: replay_window(scratch / 'census-dry', july_test.fake_jev(Everything())))\n   124\t    proposed = sum(len(o['proposed']) for o in result['openings with a pair shown'])\n   125\t    print('links proposed by the fake answers:', proposed)\n   126\t    return result['equal to old-2'] and result['link rows written'] == 0 and proposed > 0\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tdef census(scratch, draw, ledger_path):\n   130\t    \"\"\"One draw of the link decisions over the window: each link job sent to Jev as poc-v119 builds it, through the comparison runs'\n   131\t    reservation ledger (`july_test.budget_module`: Jev reserved at its published 64K limit for each of its three attempts); the\n   132\t    writer is handed no proposed link, so no link row is written and every later request stays old-2's (the pass checks equality at the\n   133\t    end). Several draws share one ledger, created by the first.\"\"\"\n   134\t    budget = july_test.budget_module()\n   135\t    if not Path(ledger_path).exists():\n   136\t        raise SystemExit('the ledger does not exist: create it first (budget_replay.py --init-ledger L --ceiling 0.10)')\n   137\t    if budget.SharedLedger(str(ledger_path)).read()['ceiling'] > CENSUS_CEILING:\n   138\t        raise SystemExit(f'the ledger ceiling is above ${CENSUS_CEILING}: refused')\n   139\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(ledger_path))\n   140\t    budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   141\t    paid = budget.BudgetTransport(ledger)\n   142\t    result = without_links(lambda: replay_window(scratch / f'census-{draw}', paid))\n   143\t    print('ledger:', ledger.read())\n   144\t    return result['equal to old-2'] and result['link rows written'] == 0\n   145\t\n   146\t\n   147\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   148\t    command, scratch = sys.argv[1], Path(sys.argv[2])\n   149\t    if command == 'neither':\n   150\t        sys.exit(0 if neither(scratch) else 1)\n   151\t    if command == 'census-dry':\n   152\t        sys.exit(0 if census_dry(scratch) else 1)\n   153\t    if command == 'census':\n   154\t        sys.exit(0 if census(scratch, sys.argv[3], Path(sys.argv[4])) else 1)\n   155\t    raise SystemExit(f'unknown command {command}')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The whole-window measurement of the linking version: design, version 1 (D699; for council review before any send)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex chose A (D699, \"continue\"): measure poc-v119 over the whole release window (2026-07-01..09-20, 1,884 articles) against poc-v118,\n     4\tthe measurement designed with the council at $0 first; the paid send waits for the council's pass and a ceiling Alex names. He was told\n     5\tthe measurement would answer four questions, in his order:\n     6\t1. over the whole window, do related number questions still contradict each other;\n     7\t2. which questions did the matching step link, and is any link wrong;\n     8\t3. does the self-made market reference (the system's own figure presented as the market's, `self-reference/RESULT.md`) become rarer;\n     9\t4. does any other question get worse.\n    10\t\n    11\t## 1. The shape: old-2 continued with links\n    12\t\n    13\tEvery request the linking version builds byte-equal to a request old-2 sent is answered with old-2's answer (each sequence works on its\n    14\town copy of old-2's archive); only the requests the links change are bought: the link questions (Jev) and the judgements of a question\n    15\tthat reads a linked question. This is the July test's method (`../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md`)\n    16\tover the whole window.\n    17\t\n    18\tWhy this shape and not an independent forward run:\n    19\t- **Question 4 is answered by construction and checked by code.** No other request carries a judgement of another question:\n    20\t  the extraction request shows open questions with their takes lines (`placement.question_lines`, `placement.takes`: key and group\n    21\t  only); Jev's matching state and thesis text show the question, its ladder and its first two pieces of evidence\n    22\t  (`jev_matching.candidate_state`, `thesis_text`, `matching.describe_view`); a judgement shows its own evidence, its own previous\n    23\t  conclusion, the theme block and its dependencies (`judging.build_prompt`). Linking writes only asset-to-asset rows (D695), so a\n    24\t  changed judgement reaches only the questions that read it. The July test confirmed it: three days, 39 bought calls, every other\n    25\t  request answered from the archive. The code check: every judgement of a question outside the reading chains is equal, row for row,\n    26\t  to old-2's.\n    27\t- **The links' effect is not buried in sampling noise.** A fresh run re-samples 1,884 extractions and about 1,600 judgements; the\n    28\t  questions opened and their evidence would differ from old-2's for reasons that have nothing to do with links.\n    29\t- **Cost:** only the readers' judgements and the link questions are bought (section 6), not the ~$9 of a fresh run.\n    30\t\n    31\tWhat this shape cannot show, stated with the result: how the link step behaves on question sets another draw would open (only old-2's\n    32\topenings are asked); a fresh run's cost and timing.\n    33\t\n    34\t## 2. The $0 proof that nothing else changes: the `neither` pass\n    35\t\n    36\t`window_test.py neither`: poc-v119 from an empty ledger over the whole window, every link question answered \"neither\" by a fake Jev,\n    37\tevery other request from old-2's archive, anything else stops the pass. An answer old-2's own run refused (the archive keeps it under a\n    38\t`:refused:` suffix, four judge answers) is given back once, so the code refuses it again and the stored retry follows; without that,\n    39\tthe first pass stopped at 07-13 (v7, whose 07-13 judgement was a retry). The pass must end equal to old-2's finished store on views,\n    40\tkeys, rungs, evidence, links, judgements, switches, successions and dependencies (`rebuild_control.compare`), and it lists every\n    41\topening with the pairs shown and which are eligible under D695.\n    42\t\n    43\tResult (`neither.log`, `neither-census.json`; 375 seconds): **equal to old-2 in every table** (43 questions, 5,102 evidence items,\n    44\t6,306 evidence links, 1,616 judgements, 137 rungs, 44 switches, 2 successions, 0 dependencies; last completed seq 1884 in both); the\n    45\tfour refusals met again and none left unmet. The version asks link questions at **14 openings** (every new number question from v2 at\n    46\tseq 8 to v36 at seq 1262), **105 eligible pairs** in 14 jobs: each new number question against every earlier open number question of\n    47\tthe company (1, 2, ... 14 pairs; themes and yes/no questions are not eligible, D695). Openings with pairs:\n    48\t\n    49\t| seq | new question | pairs |\n    50\t|---|---|---|\n    51\t| 8 | v2 commitments for customer and cloud-provider guarantees, FY2027 | 1 |\n    52\t| 49 | v8 stand-alone CPU revenue FY2027 | 2 |\n    53\t| 62 | v9 Data Center revenue FY2027 | 3 |\n    54\t| 148 | v14 total revenue FY2027 | 4 |\n    55\t| 206 | v15 supply commitments, FY2027 report | 5 |\n    56\t| 265 | v16 total CPU revenue FY2027 | 6 |\n    57\t| 321 | v17 total revenue growth FY2028 | 7 |\n    58\t| 534 | v21 total revenue growth FY2027 | 8 |\n    59\t| 746 | v28 gross margin FY2027 | 9 |\n    60\t| 821 | v29 equity investment commitments, FY2027 report | 10 |\n    61\t| 1029 | v32 Poolside licence payment commitment | 11 |\n    62\t| 1102 | v33 gross margin FY2028 | 12 |\n    63\t| 1238 | v35 total revenue FY2028 | 13 |\n    64\t| 1262 | v36 MediaTek convertible-bond investment | 14 |\n    65\t\n    66\t## 3. Before any judgement is bought: the link decisions over the window\n    67\t\n    68\t**The July answers were close to a coin flip.** In each linked sequence Jev answered the 07-10 opening of v14 (total revenue FY2027)\n    69\tagainst v9 (Data Center FY2027): \"v9 reads v14\" 0.52, 0.54, 0.51; \"v14 reads v9\" 0.47, 0.45, 0.48. The rule takes Jev's choice at\n    70\t0.5 or more (`links.THRESHOLD`), so a shift of 0.02 gives no link or the opposite link. The same opening's v14–v8 (stand-alone CPU)\n    71\tpair: \"v14 reads v8\" 0.47, 0.46, 0.44 (below the line), \"neither\" ~0.40. JULY-RESULT.md reported the link \"chosen in 3 of 3\" without\n    72\tthese margins; this is added to it.\n    73\t\n    74\t**Mechanism (prompt audit, `links.READS_CRITERIA`):** \"candidate_reads_thesis\" covers \"a part read against its whole ... or a\n    75\tquantity read against another it depends on\"; for a total against its own segment, both readings fit: the segment is a part of the\n    76\ttotal, and the total depends on the segment. The documents carry both: D537 and council R name \"data-center revenue reading total\n    77\trevenue\" (a part reads its whole); PRD 06 (line 134, D368 by D208) says a historical seed's supported root reads its supporting\n    78\tdrivers. Verdict: **abstract** (one class, two directions with a source each).\n    79\t\n    80\t**The census** (`window_test.py census`, Jev only): the same whole-window pass with each link job sent to Jev as poc-v119 builds it\n    81\tand the writer handed no link, so no row is written and every later request stays old-2's (checked by the same equality). Three draws\n    82\tshare one reservation ledger, ceiling $0.10 (Jev reserved at its published 64K limit for each of its three attempts, as in July).\n    83\tIts $0 checks: `census-dry` (every eligible pair answered \"the THESIS reads the CANDIDATE\", sign together: 28 jobs, 105 links\n    84\tproposed, 0 written, equal to old-2 in every table, `census-dry.log`); the mutant (the same fake answers with links written) stops on\n    85\t07-01 at the first reader judgement, which misses the archive (`census-mutant.log`). Cost: 14 READS jobs of 1 to 14 questions per\n    86\tdraw plus the SIGN jobs of what passes; Jev input at $0.042 per million tokens.\n    87\tRead for every eligible pair: the answer and its probabilities in each draw; whether the chosen direction and sign are right under\n    88\tthe criterion's own examples; whether the decision is the same in 3 of 3 draws.\n    89\t\n    90\t**What the census decides:**\n    91\t- every link chosen in some draw is chosen in 3 of 3 draws with a winning margin of at least 0.10 over the next class, and is right:\n    92\t  the run goes ahead on the current wording;\n    93\t- otherwise the unstable or wrong class goes to the council before any judgement is bought. A wording that fixes the part-and-whole\n    94\t  direction picks between two sourced readings (D537 against D368/PRD 06 line 134): that choice changes what the system does and goes\n    95\t  to Alex with its options and a recommendation.\n    96\t\n    97\t## 4. The paid run (after the census, the council and Alex's ceiling)\n    98\t\n    99\t- **Linked, three sequences:** poc-v119, each on its own copy of old-2's archive and an empty ledger, the whole window. Jev's link\n   100\t  answers are not byte-stable (the July probabilities moved by up to 0.03), so the three may choose different links; each is read.\n   101\t- **Control, three sequences:** poc-v118 on its own archive copy with the judge rows of every reader of the linked sequences (their\n   102\t  union) retired from the seq of that reader's first link, so their judgements are fresh samples of the same requests old-2 sent.\n   103\t- **old-2's stored path** is a fourth control path, labelled: v9's self-made reference was found on it, so it is not a neutral draw.\n   104\t- Order: the three linked sequences first (they decide the readers), then the three controls. One shared reservation ledger under the\n   105\t  ceiling Alex names; a refused reservation or a stop makes the comparison inconclusive.\n   106\t- Each sequence uses the comparison runs' budget transport with July's settlement (cache writes at 1.25x), and an allow-list before\n   107\t  it: a sequence may buy only link questions and the judgements of its readers (linked) or of the retired readers (control); any other\n   108\t  request that misses the archive stops that sequence (July's latch).\n   109\t\n   110\t## 5. Reading rule (to be frozen before the paid send)\n   111\t\n   112\tPer linked pair (reader R reads T), over every day R is judged; scored by Claude first, then by a blind reader under shuffled labels.\n   113\t- **A, the links:** each link committed in a linked sequence, read with both questions and ladders: right or wrong (relation,\n   114\t  direction, sign).\n   115\t- **B, contradiction:** for a part read against its whole, R's implied outcome above T's implied outcome, or leaving less for the rest\n   116\t  than the reported rest of the latest quarter carried over the remaining quarters (July's rule C generalised); for another relation,\n   117\t  R's implied outcome on the side of its ladder that T's conclusion and the sign rule out, stated as such in the reasons.\n   118\t- **C, self-made reference:** `self-reference/reference_census.py`'s three measures on every reader judgement, linked against controls.\n   119\t- **D, harm:** a reader calling T's forecast a market figure or evidence (grounding error); first-attempt refusals; failed articles;\n   120\t  any judgement outside the reading chains differing from old-2's (code).\n   121\t- **Pass line (proposed, for the council):** every committed link right by both readers; B: linked days in contradiction at most half\n   122\t  the controls' mean, with the controls showing at least two (else \"not tested\"); C: linked at most the controls' mean; D: no\n   123\t  grounding error and no failed article in the linked arm, refusals at most the controls' plus two, every other judgement equal to\n   124\t  old-2's.\n   125\t\n   126\t## 6. Cost (estimate, to be priced from the census)\n   127\t\n   128\tLink questions: Jev input at $0.042 per million tokens, July's two jobs cost under $0.001. Reader judgements: old-2's stored v9\n   129\tjudgements cost about $0.003 each at published rates (July's `price`); a reader judged about 70 times over the window, plus the days a\n   130\tchanged T queues it. Priced from the census's readers and old-2's stored judgement tokens before the ceiling question.\n   131\t\n   132\t## 7. State × event (the harness; the product path's rows are DESIGN.md §6 of the dependency design)\n   133\t\n   134\t| Event | Outcome |\n   135\t|---|---|\n   136\t| a request outside the allow-list misses the archive | the sequence stops (latch), final, reported; the comparison is inconclusive if any sequence stops |\n   137\t| a request old-2's run refused | its stored answer is given back once; the check refuses it again; the stored retry follows |\n   138\t| a fresh reader answer is refused twice | the article or the day fails as in the product; the sequence stops; reported |\n   139\t| a link closes a circle | one correction per link (product path); a persistent circle fails the article: the sequence stops |\n   140\t| a reservation would pass the ceiling | refused, the ledger stops, every sequence stops: inconclusive |\n   141\t| a process dies | the sequence is final (never resumed); the reservation stays counted |\n   142\t| two sequences at once | separate folders and archive copies; one shared ledger under its lock |\n   143\t\n   144\t## 8. Prior decisions\n   145\t\n   146\tD694 (A), D695 (number questions only), D696 (reservation from request size), D697/D698 (the July proof and result), D699 (A for the\n   147\twhole window), D537 (part reads whole) and PRD 06 line 134 (D368/D208: root reads drivers), D677 (no paid work unless Alex funds a run\n   148\twith a written path to passing: D699 is that funding; this document is the path), D667 (three draws for totals; D431's same-day rule\n   149\tdoes not apply: every sequence reads the same stored articles), D449 (a crash stops the run).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
