{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10482,10514p'; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py | sed -n '43,54p;454,470p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/writing.py | sed -n '113,131p'\"","aggregated_output":" 10482\t## D697 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the $0 proof of the linking version; the July comparison is sent (D694 (c), D696)\n 10483\t\n 10484\t- **The council** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/`, Codex thread `01a1fcdb…`): design rounds 4–8\n 10485\t  (NOT READY four times, READY TO BUILD in round 8), proof rounds 9–12 (NOT READY three times: budget bounds, exact dry-run checks,\n 10486\t  the latch, the send loop, the starting-state check, the selection record, cache-write settlement; READY TO SEND in round 12 under\n 10487\t  D696). Every finding was taken; the record of each is `PROOF.md`.\n 10488\t- **The proof** (`PROOF.md`, $0): suite 378 passed; 7 of 7 mutants caught; the July starting state equal to old-2; poc-v119 without\n 10489\t  links reproduces the prefix; the archive test; the dry run's 42 checks; the stop paths; the latch race; historical settlements within\n 10490\t  31.2% of their reservations; preflight; price about $0.085 for six sequences; the reading rule frozen (`reading-rule.md`).\n 10491\t- **Sent:** `july_test.py send` into `poc/data/july-link-test-2026-11-21/`, ceiling $0.15, by Alex's A (D694) and D696.\n 10492\t\n 10493\t## D698 · 2026-11-21 · The July test of the linking version passes its frozen rule; next steps go to Alex\n 10494\t\n 10495\t- **Result** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/JULY-RESULT.md`, $0.0689 of $0.15): in all three linked\n 10496\t  sequences the matcher chose and the writer committed \"v9 reads v14\" at seq 148 and nothing else. Linked sequences meeting A–D: 3 of 3\n 10497\t  (Claude), 2 of 3 (blind Codex reader); controls meeting A–C: 1 of 3 (Claude), 0 of 3 (reader); no refusal, no grounding error. PASS by\n 10498\t  both readers; their two disagreements (control-1's unsized uplift, linked-2's \"stated bound\") do not move it.\n 10499\t- **Disclosed with it:** the stored annual contradiction did not recur in the fresh controls (the total rose to ~$411B on 07-12); the\n 10500\t  controls' remaining contradictions are in the implied second half, which rule C cannot see; the verdict rests on B read as written\n 10501\t  for two controls; coherence is not accuracy; one pair, three days.\n 10502\t- **Open:** PRD 06 still says the default matcher is not asked for dependencies (true of poc-v118, the product); it changes with the\n 10503\t  decision that makes a linking version the product. The sourced-reference change (D693) waits for a longer linked run.\n 10504\t\n 10505\t## D699 · 2026-11-21 · Alex continues with A: the whole-window measurement of the linking version, designed with the council at $0 first\n 10506\t\n 10507\t- **Alex's words** (2026-11-21), replying to the next-step question after D698 (A, recommended: run poc-v119 over 07-01..09-20 once,\n 10508\t  about $9 as one poc-v118 run cost, its measurement designed with the council at $0 before any send: whether related number questions\n 10509\t  still contradict each other, which links the matcher chose and whether any is wrong, whether the self-made market reference becomes\n 10510\t  rarer, whether other questions get worse; then decide whether the new version replaces the product. B: stop, poc-v118 stays): \"continue\".\n 10511\t- **Decided (Alex):** A. The $0 design and its council come first. The ~$9 was an estimate, not a ceiling: the paid send waits for the\n 10512\t  council's pass and a ceiling Alex names. poc-v118 stays the product until a later decision.\n 10513\t- **Next:** the design (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/`), its $0 proofs, council rounds, then the ceiling question to Alex.\n    43\tdef judged_view(request):\n    44\t    \"\"\"The thesis a judge request is about (its user text begins \"Thesis <id> (\"), or None for any other request.\"\"\"\n    45\t    if 'messages' not in request:\n    46\t        return None\n    47\t    text = request['messages'][-1]['content']\n    48\t    return text.split(' ', 2)[1] if text.startswith('Thesis v') else None\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef is_link_request(request):\n    52\t    questions = request.get('questions') or {}\n    53\t    return bool(questions) and all(qid.startswith(('reads__', 'sign__')) for qid in questions)\n    54\t\n   454\t    written = min(tokens_in - cached, written)\n   455\t    plain = tokens_in - cached - written\n   456\t    return (plain * price_in + cached * price_in * model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + written * price_in * CACHE_WRITE_SHARE + tokens_out * price_out) / 1e6\n   457\t\n   458\t\n   459\tdef budget_module():\n   460\t    \"\"\"The comparison runs' budget transport, with this harness's settlement (cache writes at their published rate) and Jev's\n   461\t    reservation at its published per-request limit for each of its attempts; the module is loaded for this harness alone.\"\"\"\n   462\t    import importlib.util\n   463\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('budget_replay_july', REPO / 'clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py')\n   464\t    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n   465\t    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n   466\t    module.llm_cost = settled_llm_cost\n   467\t    original_jev_estimate = module.jev_estimate\n   468\t    module.jev_estimate = lambda request: max(original_jev_estimate(request),\n   469\t                                              module.jev.ATTEMPTS * JEV_REQUEST_TOKENS * model.PRICES[request['model']][0] / 1e6)\n   470\t    return module\n   113\tdef write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass, *, proposed_links=None):\n   114\t    \"\"\"Write atomically within the caller's transaction; the caller commits the completion marker with it. proposed_links: the reading\n   115\t    links the link step chose (views/links.py, D694), written after the new views exist; None writes none.\"\"\"\n   116\t    if not conn.in_transaction:\n   117\t        conn.execute('begin immediate')\n   118\t    conn.execute('savepoint view_write')\n   119\t    try:\n   120\t        store.ensure_writable_columns(conn)\n   121\t        result = _write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   122\t        if proposed_links:\n   123\t            result.links = _write_links(conn, seq, proposed_links, result)\n   124\t    except Exception:\n   125\t        conn.execute('rollback to view_write')\n   126\t        conn.execute('release view_write')\n   127\t        raise\n   128\t    conn.execute('release view_write')\n   129\t    return result\n   130\t\n   131\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
