{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"The census is **not ready to send**. The $0 replay shows that link proposals can be recorded without changing the stored answers. But the proposed gate can pass if no links are chosen, and the parallel launcher does not fully enforce its stated budget and crash rules.\n\n## 1. What the paired replay can answer\n\nThe design is sound for a **conditional comparison on old-2’s questions and evidence**. It can show which links the matcher chooses on that trajectory, whether those links reduce contradictions or self-made references, and whether any unrelated daily judgement changes. It cannot establish what a fresh run would open or whether the same gains hold on a different set of questions. Equality outside the reading chains is a check for unintended changes in this replay, rather than a general finding about product quality. Also, the archive checks canonical request identity. For Luna, that differs from checking the exact bytes sent. [Whole-window design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:11) · [Request identity and lookup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:245) · [Verification rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:177)\n\n- **Extraction and matching:** I found no route from a changed judgement into either request. Extraction renders question text, metadata, keys and groups. Jev renders candidate evidence and the stored question’s card, ladder, status, succession, groups and first two evidence pieces. The link chooser uses those same builders. [Extraction question lines](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/placement.py:19) · [Jev builders](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:56) · [Stored question card](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:161) · [Link chooser](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:229)\n- **Closing, themes and the queue:** Closing reads the last rung and writes it into the closing reason. The close date is driven by the due date and there is no closing model call. Themes already carry other questions’ conclusions. The theme update marker compares judgement IDs, although the IDs themselves stay out of the prompt. Check the marker and compare unrelated judgements by question and day, since added reader judgements can shift row IDs. A committed link can queue an existing reader, and a changed conclusion can add readers further down the chain. A reader’s own prior citations and judgement dates also change the evidence shown on later days. [Closing](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/pull.py:11) · [Theme update marker](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:77) · [Reader queued on write](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:153) · [Daily queue](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:287) · [Evidence shown](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:42)\n- **Idea routes:** The broader claim has a counterexample. Idea mapping receives candidates’ judged positions, and the detailed route and summary can receive their reasons. The daily replay does not invoke those routes. Scope §1’s claim to that replay and leave idea quality outside this measurement. [Idea briefs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:120) · [Mapping request](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:258) · [Summary request](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:341) · [Daily replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/replay.py:119)\n\n## 2. What the census should decide\n\nI read calls 8738 and 8739 in all three July archives and rebuilt both seq-148 requests from old-2. Both hashes matched. The winning direction margins were **0.05, 0.09 and 0.03**. The `together` sign scores were **0.94, 0.95 and 0.94**. The fragility is in the direction. A two-point swing can flip the closest draw, and a smaller drop below 0.50 can suppress it. Those are margins in the returned scores. They do not estimate how often a new run will flip. [July margin record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/JULY-RESULT.md:38) · [Product threshold](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:202)\n\nThe prompt gives the model room to read “depends on” in both directions. The governing sources are narrower than §3 suggests. D537 identifies a case where the segment needed the total’s conclusion. D368 item 4 and PRD 06 line 134 describe **historical seed arrows**. They supply no reverse rule for a newly chosen number link. [READS criteria](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:22) · [D537](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6457) · [D368](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3973) · [PRD 06](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/06-views.md:134)\n\nA Jev-only census is the cheapest way to learn how widespread the direction problem is before buying judgements. The proposed gate needs a known positive, though. Three draws that choose nothing pass it, and three draws can repeat the same wrong decision. Moreover, the exact July request already misses the proposed 0.10 bar in all three samples. Reuse those samples. Register required links, valid abstentions and wrong links before reading the remaining answers. Count missed required links and sign abstentions, and use the margin as a fragility flag. If 0.10 remains a hard requirement, the current wording already fails it on the known positive. A further census can size that failure class. [Proposed gate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:80) · [Sampler and cheapest-test rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:332)\n\n## 3. Census harness and budget\n\n**Suppressing the write works within the fixed replay.** Passing `proposed_links=None` bypasses both the dependency insert and the extra `changed` entry. `round.run` still records the proposal and an empty committed-link list. The selector’s graph check runs earlier. On this trajectory the 14 eligible openings occur at distinct article sequences, each with one eligible new candidate, and there are no stored edges. The proposals at each step therefore cannot form a cycle. The census cannot measure cycle corrections once earlier links are allowed to persist. The 105-proposal dry run and the mutant provide the right structural proof. Describe the equality as equality on the **compared columns**. The helper compares nine projections, rather than every field of every table. [Writer and savepoint](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:113) · [Selection and write records](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:153) · [Graph check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:242) · [Dry run](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/census-dry.log:1) · [Mutant](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/census-mutant.log:1) · [Equality queries](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py:37)\n\n**Only link jobs can reach the budget transport through the current replay callback.** Other misses get one of the four recorded refusals or stop. The harness still needs to verify the expected READS manifest and conditional SIGN coverage before counting a draw as complete. Its current return check accepts equality and zero written links alone. Carry over July’s harness-only store marker and lock so ordinary replay cannot write to the same store. Record preflight for the whole-window inputs before sending. [Transport filter](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:44) · [Census completion check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:129) · [July store protections](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:37) · [Preflight requirement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:182)\n\n**$0.10 can be a stop, but it does not guarantee three complete draws.** Three concurrent $0.008064 reservations occupy $0.024192. Up to 84 READS/SIGN jobs can run across three draws. Price the expected settlements with that live reservation headroom and declare a budget-truncated census incomplete. Fix two launcher gaps before sending. The ceiling check accepts `NaN`, which I verified also lets the ledger grant a reservation after $0.20 has been spent. Require a finite, positive, approved ceiling. Also register each draw’s launcher with the shared ledger. The installed stop gate detects a dead **registered** launcher, and `census` never registers one. D699 authorizes the design work and requires Alex to name the ceiling before a send. [Census launcher](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:129) · [Reservation and launcher registration](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:126) · [D699](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10505)\n\n## 4. For the later judgement-send review\n\n- **Pair the fresh controls to the actual change.** Retiring the union of readers in every control can freshen a question before its first affected judgement, or freshen a question that stayed archived in its linked counterpart. Pair each control with its linked sequence and retire that reader’s original and retry requests from its first affected daily judgement. Keep the shared prefix and unaffected target answers fixed. Report linked-only judgement days separately and document any fresh link choices that differ from the census. Keep old-2 as a labelled historical baseline outside the fresh-control mean. Run the fresh calls together to limit provider drift. The stored article dates do not control when a provider samples its answers. [Proposed arms](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:97) · [July fresh controls](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:31) · [Fresh-control requirement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:336)\n- **Separate contradiction, sourcing and harm.** For comparable part–whole amounts, compare matching scopes and periods, distinguish definite contradictions from overlapping ranges, and use a remainder only where the evidence establishes a floor. Carrying the latest quarter’s remainder into future quarters is a forecast assumption. A directional sign says which move is more likely and supplies no hard bound. For self-made references, trace the amount to an outside statement with the right scope. The current text scan would clear a number copied from the linked forecast merely because it appeared in the request. Retain July’s arithmetic and material-assumption check so two forecasts becoming consistent cannot hide a newly unsupported forecast. [Proposed rules B–D](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:110) · [Sign definition](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:32) · [Reference scan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference_census.py:49) · [July reading rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md:5)\n- **Freeze the comparison unit and its baseline before sending.** Compare rates on common question-pair dates, report missing and extra days separately, and count a judgement-level harm once even when it reads several links. Define pass, fail and inconclusive for zero links, too few comparable dates and no recurring control contradiction. Check how often the proposed halving rule would declare an improvement when comparing controls with controls. The daily answers inherit earlier answers, so the three whole trajectories are the independent repeats. July already showed the practical consequence: the original annual contradiction did not recur in any fresh control. [Proposed pass line](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:121) · [July result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/JULY-RESULT.md:23) · [AGENTS §7.3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:332)\n\nFor the census, the blocking changes are to register a gate that detects missing links, reuse the exact July samples, prove a complete draw under the launcher’s isolation and shared-stop rules, record preflight, and obtain Alex’s ceiling. The judgement comparison gets its own review after that census.\n\n**NOT READY**"}}
